  "answer": "I'll look through the storefront cart API and how store merchant settings are read so the per-line quantity cap can be enforced without a restart.The cap belongs on the cart write paths, read from merchant configuration on each request so a store change applies immediately. I'll reject any line that would go over that limit before the cart is saved.The storefront cart write paths now reject a line that would go above the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` merchant setting (99 when that setting is absent). The value is read on each request, so a change applies without a restart. `POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi` return HTTP 400 and leave the cart unchanged. A quantity of 0 still removes the line.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 and an unchanged cart when a line exceeds the limit\", \"that a configuration change applies without restart\"], \"missing\": [\"a cart API test or fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and asserts the rejected request\"]}",
